From f04342565c0963f466c9bae21dc1b0d9158bab44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TruthProbe <truthprobe@local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:40:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] feat(truthprobe): probe providers and enable logprobs
 automatically

Adding a provider key no longer needs an environment variable.

* `opencode.truthprobe` plugin listens on `http.request`, where both the
  model and the authorised URL are visible, and enqueues the event. A
  single worker fiber sends one fixed one-token probe
  (`"ping"`, `max_tokens: 1`, `logprobs: true`) so the model response
  never waits for the check and user data never leaves the machine.
* The verdict is cached in `<data>/truthprobe/capabilities.json`
  (ok/ignored/rejected/unsupported 7d, auth 1h, transport errors are not
  cached) and replayed at startup, so a known-good endpoint collects
  logprobs from the first request of the next run.
* `capabilities.logprobs` is set through the model transform, and the
  `ai` package reads the same cache via `OPENCODE_TRUTHPROBE_CACHE`
  (standard data directory as a fallback), so the protocol asks for
  logprobs without any manual configuration.
* Provider-level fallback: any fresh `ok` entry of the same provider
  counts, because logprobs support is an endpoint property and aliases
  or variants must not hide the badge.
* `mergeCapabilities` now carries `logprobs`, which it used to drop.
* Disable with `OPENCODE_TRUTHPROBE_PROBE=off`.

Tests: 32 capability cases plus the existing 45 scoring/protocol cases.
