From a478531b342afc1a07626aafcd1e085543cbaef2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: truthprobe <truthprobe@local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:21:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] fix(truthprobe): keep logprobs that arrive without text,
 align tokens, always publish a verdict

- ai: buffer token logprobs in parser state; gateways send them in a separate
  chunk with an empty delta, so every text chunk looked like it had none
- core: publish the truthprobe verdict even when no tokens arrived, so the UI
  can say 'unavailable' out loud instead of rendering nothing
- core: score reasoning-token logprobs and fall back to them for the answer
- core: align tokens to the answer text instead of concatenating blindly, so
  sentence-level scores survive internal tokens such as </think>
- core: one topK for both probe and live request; 'off' now disables the probe
- core: keep single-character CJK/kana/hangul tokens as content
- session-ui: show 'first-token' and 'answer' confidence always, with reason
- tui: rename the first-token line to match what it measures
- server: answer /api/info in every state so the desktop client can connect
